SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 GMT: Digital Democracy Edinburgh 2027: Call for Prop
 osals (TICTeC\, mySociety\, AI4CI\, Scottish Government)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 15 Nov 2026 at 23:59 GMT.\n\nDigital Democracy Edinburgh
  is a two-day conference from mySociety's TICTeC (The Impacts of Civic Tec
 hnology) series\, run with the AI for Collective Intelligence (AI4CI) Rese
 arch Hub\, the Scottish Government and the Edinburgh Futures Institute\, f
 or researchers\, policy makers and practitioners reimagining technology fo
 r more resilient democracies.\n\nOrganisation: mySociety (TICTeC) with the
  AI for Collective Intelligence (AI4CI) Hub\, the Scottish Government and 
 the Edinburgh Futures Institute\, University of Edinburgh\nLocation: Edinb
 urgh Futures Institute\, Edinburgh\, Scotland\, UK. Primarily in-person\, 
 with a limited number of remote presentation slots.\nAward: NO GUARANTEED 
 CASH\, listed as an exception at the editor's request: accepted speakers g
 et complimentary conference registration\, and a limited number of travel 
 scholarships are available for speakers who could otherwise not attend (pr
 iority to applicants from ODA-eligible countries and under-29s\; amount no
 t published). Free to submit.\nDuration: Two-day conference\, 11-12 March 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://tictec.mysociety.org/event/digital-democracy-edinbu
 rgh/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tictec.mysociety.org/event/digital-democracy-edinburgh/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Edinburgh Futures Institute\, Edinburgh\, Scotland\, UK. Primarily
  in-person\, with a limited number of remote presentation slots.
END:VEVENT
